  "tagline": "MPP OLAP database with a fast vectorized engine, real-time upserts and native lakehouse queries.",
  "description": "StarRocks is an open-source MPP analytical database (a 2020 fork of Apache Doris, now a Linux Foundation project) with a C++ vectorized engine and a cost-based optimizer that handles multi-table joins well. It serves both its own primary-key tables, which support real-time upserts from Kafka or Flink, and external Iceberg, Hudi, Delta and Hive tables directly, with async materialized views that transparently rewrite queries. Shared-data mode stores data on object storage with local caching. It is a strong pick for joins-heavy, high-concurrency analytics; the frontend/backend architecture and MySQL-flavoured SQL take some getting used to.",
